decided, so it is not decided twice

one cur per tmux window — $home/.config/sys/cur/@3 — and one m for the
machine. it is per workspace; memory is one.

the pane is too small a unit: fm in one and the shell in another could
tell each other nothing, which is the problem this started from. the
machine is too big: two projects trade this between them. the window is
already the unit and the layout says so — spawn splits into the current
one, the shell holds its left, and everything beside it was spawned from
there. outside tmux the id is none and nothing else changes.

the id costs c one fork, $TMUX_PANE names a pane and not its window. fm
asks once at startup. dead windows leave a stale file of one line each;
not worth collecting.

ask with -t $TMUX_PANE or do not ask. an untargeted tmux display answers
about the session's current window, not the pane running the command,
and a detached or background pane then reads and writes another window's
this. it looks right until there are two windows.
`sh/p:/pane=(-t $TMUX_PANE)/` already does it that way; the same goes
for set -w @cur, which lands on the wrong window unqualified.

cur unset is the cwd, resolved once inside c, so o with no argument
stays what the readme says it is.

m is what was said, not every twitch: c appends, a view writing cur does
not. fm writes on every j, and at one line per keypress back is
unusable. still one writer.

cur is written temp then renamed. between truncate and write a reader
gets an empty address, and an empty address is a verb with no noun.

c prints its reading always, sets cur only when that reading exists;
nothing reads its status. so e newfile falls back to the raw word and
still makes a file, and ed's save is what lands it in cur — the same
rule as mv and mkdir, cur follows what the verb made.

c prints a path, never an address. `{c} is how every tool not ours gets
the pronoun — git add `{c}, wc -l `{c} — and it has to be a filename
each of them will take. git add foo.go:12 is not one. the line stays in
cur for the two verbs that read it, and the address whole is m 0, which
is cur already and so costs no word.

